> *** In what sense is "read" not present?  It is one of the value in the variable column, and it was one of the column names in matrix produced by ddply

It is not present as a column name. You cannot just pull out some rows
and put them in columns. It's all or nothing.

>
> ***Here's a simple example with no ply functions.  Essentially I'm trying to reconstruct the original df from the melted data:
>     msmall <- matrix(101:106, nrow=2)
>     colnames(msmall) <- c("ID", "X", "Y")
>     df <- as.data.frame(msmall)
>     head(df)
>     dd <- melt(df, measure=c("X", "Y"))
>     head(dd)
>     x <- cast(dd, ID~X+Y)
>
> Results:
>>     head(df)
>    ID   X   Y
> 1 101 103 105
> 2 102 104 106
>>     dd <- melt(df, measure=c("X", "Y"))
>>     head(dd)
>    ID variable value
> 1 101        X   103
> 2 102        X   104
> 3 101        Y   105
> 4 102        Y   106
>>     x <- cast(dd, ID~X+Y)
> Error: Casting formula contains variables not found in molten data: X, Y

It just doesn't work that way. The variables in your casting formula
have to exist in the data.frame.

x <- cast(dd, ID ~ variable)

